text @[Gentleman]
text Will you allow me to explain?
text Everyone turns to the gentleman as he speaks in his gentle voice.
sound EEC.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text This suitcase did belong to the Ichinoses.
sound EED.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text We know that they brought it into the cabin as a carry-on.
sound EEE.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text And unfortunately, they were caught in an accident...
text The gentleman looks down at the open suitcase.
sound EEF.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text What happened after that is merely supposition.
sound EEG.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text The suitcase must have been thrown out of the airplane from the shock of the crash. Because it was light, it didn't sink with the rest of the airplane.
sound EEH.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text It must have floated in the water for some time.
sound EEI.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text The suitcase eventually washed ashore in some faraway country.
sound EEJ.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text The accident must have been long forgotten by the time that happened.
sound EEK.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text Someone must have found the suitcase and opened it.
sound EEL.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text Inside, they found a teddy bear and an envelope.
sound EEM.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text They could have discarded it or even kept it for themselves.
sound EEN.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text But the one who found it did not do that. That person must have entrusted the suitcase to someone else.
sound EEO.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text They must have thought that the owner had lost something very precious.
sound EEP.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text And the suitcase was passed from hand to hand, from nation to nation.
text No one can say anything.
text When he sees us staring, the gentleman laughs bashfully.
sound EEQ.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text I don't think my conjecture is very far from the truth.
sound EER.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text I have an acquaintance who knows quite a lot about minerals. I had him test the sand inside the suitcase.
sound EES.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text It's most likely from a desert deep in the heart of Africa.
sound EET.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text I cannot even begin to imagine the path the suitcase must have taken through there.
sound EEU.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text But there are indications that people have tried to repair both the stuffed animal and the suitcase.
text I look at the weathered suitcase again.
text It looks like a traveler who has just returned home from a very long trip after having many different experiences.
text Kotomi is staring at the teddy bear.
text The fake black eyes appear to be smiling at her.
sound EEV.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text There's something I want to tell you, Kotomi-kun.
text The gentleman tries to explain something.
sound EEW.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text The envelope you burned back then...
sound EEX.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text You must not have known what was inside of it.
