bgload {$strS[1000]}.jpg 55
text Kotomi lets go of the paper and it falls to the desk.
text I look at the writing.
text There are two distinct handwriting styles in the dozen or so lines that are faded and worn away here and there.
text These are the final words a mother and father wrote to their daughter.
text They must have written these words in the cabin amidst the chaos in the short time before the plane crashed into the water.
text But they don't appear to have been written in a rush or in confusion.
text There's no fear, no regret, and no despair anywhere in the messages.
text The words are written in the same calm and composed voices they used to answer their daughter's innocent questions.
text The writing is soft and round, as if they were telling their daughter where to find her afternoon snack.
text It's obvious just from looking at the suitcase.
text This suitcase must have originally held stationery and her father's other belongings. His research paper must have been in it, too.
text When they realized that they didn't have much longer to live, Kotomi's parents tossed everything out of the suitcase without hesitation.
text Then they put the stuffed animal in the case and wrote this letter together.
text They did this for Kotomi.
text They did it to give a birthday present to their precious daughter who they valued more than their own lives...
sound EG1.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text Listen, Kotomi-kun.
sound EG2.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text The research paper is right here.
sound EG3.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text What you see before you is the greatest paper the Ichinoses spent their lives completing.
text The gentleman says that proudly.
text I can tell that his eyes are moist behind his glasses.
sound EG4.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text I can guarantee you this...
sound EG5.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text I have never encountered any words more beautiful than these.
sound EG6.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text The Ichinoses...
sound EG7.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text Your father and mother...
sound EG8.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text ...had prayed only...
sound EG9.aac
text @[Gentleman]
text ...for your happiness.
music ~
delay 60
text And then...
text Kotomi touches the stuffed animal.
text She picks it up, treating it like a fragile treasure.
delay 60
jump SEEN4513_1_0.scr
